{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 28, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "## Lost in Translation (and Loving It!) - My Japan Adventure\n\nJapan. The word itself conjures images of ancient temples, bustling cityscapes, and serene gardens. And let me tell you, it absolutely lived up to the hype! \n\nMy recent trip was a whirlwind of sensory overload in the best possible way. From the moment I stepped off the plane in Tokyo, I was captivated. The neon lights of Shibuya Crossing were breathtaking, a chaotic yet organized spectacle. I spent hours wandering through the tranquil Meiji Jingu Shrine, a peaceful oasis amidst the urban sprawl.\n\nFood, of course, was a major highlight. I slurped down ramen in tiny, hole-in-the-wall restaurants, devoured delicate sushi, and indulged in fluffy okonomiyaki. Every meal was an adventure!\n\nBeyond Tokyo, I explored Kyoto, the former imperial capital. The golden Kinkaku-ji (Golden Pavilion) shimmered in the sunlight, and the bamboo forest of Arashiyama felt like stepping into another world. \n\nNavigating the public transport system was a challenge (and a source of amusement!), but the efficiency and politeness of the people made it easy. I learned a few basic Japanese phrases – \"arigato\" (thank you) became my go-to! \n\nJapan is a country of contrasts – ancient traditions coexisting with futuristic technology. It’s a place that challenges your perceptions and leaves you wanting more. I can't wait to go back!\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.002092435723170638}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": -0.1512679010629654}, {"token": "▁Translation", "logprob": -0.0005576247931458056}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.29694533348083496}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -0.0006216024048626423}, {"token": "▁Loving", "logprob": -0.0002892790944315493}, {"token": "▁It", "logprob": -0.00023946279543451965}, {"token": "!)", "logprob": -0.256867